---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import names from "../data/names.json";
import hack from "../data/hackathon.json";
const REPO = names.repo_core;
const REPO_URL = REPO;
const META = "Ethereus is an EVM agent whose spending rules, hashes and arithmetic run inside the model's own layers, where a prompt can't switch them off. Open weights, exact, replayable.";
---

<Base title="Build" description={META}>
<style>
  .hero{padding:36px 0 18px}.hero h1{margin:0;font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem);letter-spacing:-.05em;line-height:.95}.hero h1.display{font-size:clamp(2.1rem,5vw,3.2rem)}.hero p{margin:10px 0 0;max-width:60ch;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .page{max-width:var(--max-prose)}.page h2{margin:26px 0 10px;font-size:1rem;letter-spacing:-.02em}.page p,.page li{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--ink-soft);line-height:1.62}.page ul{margin:8px 0 0;padding-left:18px}
  .card{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--surface);padding:16px}
  .chips{display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:1fr}@media(min-width:560px){.chips{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
  .chip-row{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--surface)}
  .chip-row .mono{font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink)}
  .code{display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 14px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-md);background:var(--surface);font-family:"JetBrains Mono",monospace;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink);white-space:pre}
  .callout{border:1px solid var(--border);border-left-color:var(--accent);border-radius:var(--radius-md);padding:12px 14px;background:var(--surface)} .callout p{margin:0;font-size:.84rem}
</style>
<section class="wrap hero">
  <p class="kicker">Build — get to the code</p>
  <h1 class="display">Run it today.</h1>
  <p>The repo is the product. Everything on this site is sourced from what's already measured there.</p>
  <div style="margin-top:14px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href={REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View the code on GitHub →</a>
    <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">How it works</a>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="wrap"><div class="page">
  <div class="card">
    <p class="kicker" style="margin:0 0 8px">Repo</p>
    <p style="margin:0"><a href={REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mono" style="text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;text-decoration-color:var(--border)">{REPO_URL}</a></p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 0">Core research code (Qwenputer + RV32 + Ethereus firmware) lives at <span class="mono">fraserbrownirl/ethereus</span>. This site is <span class="mono">fraserbrownirl/ethereus-site</span> — frontend only, no weights, no Python.</p>
  </div>
  <h2>What runs today</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Qwenputer checkpoint on <span class="mono">Qwen3.5-4B</span>: 11 compiled layers, ~1M nonzero weights, Triton executor at ~3,700 instr/s on one L4.</li>
    <li>RV32 firmware: keccak, ABI, <span class="mono">u256</span>, EVM helpers, policy check — <span class="mono">eth-bridge.elf</span> (78 KB text / 262 KB ROM).</li>
    <li>Gate 1 passed 2026-10-31: 4,000 cases (2,000 keccak, 2,000 uint256), 0 mismatches, reference machine vs Python. Per call: keccak ≈ 24,000 instructions (19,769 per permutation), uint256 ≈ 12,000. Toolchain: riscv64-elf-gcc 16.2, picolibc. Full table in <a href="https://github.com/fraserbrownirl/ethereus/blob/main/experimental/riscv/docs/eth-bench.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">eth-bench.md</a>.</li>
    <li>Next: ABI encode/decode and the EVM interpreter on the built-in ERC-20.</li>
    <li>Language fidelity: KL ~6e-4 vs base Qwen on plain text — the model still reads and writes like itself.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Phase status <span class="mono" style="font-weight:500;color:var(--ink-faint)">· updated <span data-updated>2026-10-31</span></span></h2>
  <p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--ink-faint)">Source: <span class="mono">public/status.json</span> — fetched at runtime, so chips change without a redeploy.</p>
  <div class="chips">
    <div class="chip-row"><span class="mono">Foundation · Qwenputer + RV32</span> <span class="chip" data-phase="foundation" data-status="done"><span class="chip-dot"></span><span data-chip-label>Done</span></span></div>
    <div class="chip-row"><span class="mono">Firmware · keccak / ABI / u256 / policy</span> <span class="chip" data-phase="firmware" data-status="in progress"><span class="chip-dot"></span><span data-chip-label>In progress</span></span></div>
    <div class="chip-row"><span class="mono">Knowledge · ethskills in-state</span> <span class="chip" data-phase="knowledge" data-status="planned"><span class="chip-dot"></span><span data-chip-label>Planned</span></span></div>
    <div class="chip-row"><span class="mono">Policy gate · injection suite</span> <span class="chip" data-phase="policy_gate" data-status="planned"><span class="chip-dot"></span><span data-chip-label>Planned</span></span></div>
    <div class="chip-row"><span class="mono">Verify · on-chain proofs</span> <span class="chip" data-phase="verify" data-status="planned"><span class="chip-dot"></span><span data-chip-label>Planned</span></span></div>
    <div class="chip-row"><span class="mono">Hackathon · hosted API + traces</span> <span class="chip" data-phase="hackathon" data-status="planned"><span class="chip-dot"></span><span data-chip-label>Planned</span></span></div>
  </div>
  <h2>How to run the demo</h2>
  <span class="code">{`# from the core repo (ethereus)
git clone https://github.com/fraserbrownirl/ethereus && cd ethereus/experimental/riscv
uv sync --extra hf

# budgets + smoke gates (no GPU needed for the reference half)
uv run python -m chipformer.rv.eth --cases 2000
uv run pytest tests/test_rv_eth.py -q

# interactive (needs Qwenputer checkpoint + L4)
hf download divagr1925/Qwen3.5-4B-Qwenputer --local-dir qwenputer-rv
uv run python -m chipformer.rv.chat qwenputer-rv --firmware tests/data/rv/eth-bridge.elf \\
  --ask "Use eth: keccak of 0x1234?"`}</span>
  <p style="margin-top:10px">See <a href="https://github.com/fraserbrownirl/ethereus/blob/main/experimental/riscv/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">experimental/riscv/README.md</a> and <a href="https://github.com/divagr18/qwenputer#quickstart" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Qwenputer quickstart</a>.</p>
  <h2>Run against the API</h2>
  <p>Once the Ethereus API endpoint is live, the base URL and a sample curl appear here. [{hack.api_base_url}]</p>
  <h2>How to contribute</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the website spec at <span class="mono">docs/website-build-spec.md</span> in the core repo — it's the source of truth for any mechanism claim.</li>
    <li>Numbers come from <span class="mono">experimental/riscv/docs/eth-bench.md</span> and the Qwenputer README — the site agent never invents a number.</li>
    <li>Site PRs go to <span class="mono">fraserbrownirl/ethereus-site</span> on branch <span class="mono">feat/site-v2</span> → preview deploy → <span class="mono">main</span>.</li>
    <li>Core PRs go to <span class="mono">fraserbrownirl/ethereus</span> — keep <span class="mono">ethereus-site/</span> out of that repo.</li>
    <li>Hackathon submissions are judged from the API trace; see <a href="/hackathon">/hackathon</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</div></section>
<div style="height:28px"></div>
</Base>
